4,PDF Kulligóng: Ethnopop Artists in Kalinga at the Interstices and Margins ...,https://thecordillerareview.upb.edu.ph/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/7-Saboy_uploaded_author-corr.pdf,"Kulligóng 'encircle', under the vojóng 'peace pact system' of the Kalinga of northern Philippines, is a principle which deems the domicile of a tribal member located outside the vúgis '[original] tribal territory' a part of the tribe's jurisdiction. I propose to deploy kulligong metaphorically by applying the concept to the creative work of contemporary Kalinga ethnopop music ...","Kalinga, Mabaka Valley",Austronesian
5,"""Wiyawi Ebi"": A Study of Kalinga Vocal Music from the Philippines",https://ojs.lib.uwo.ca/index.php/notabene/article/view/22232,"Collaboration with members of the Kalinga culture enriched this work, yielding a newly expanded set of lyrics to ""Wiyawi."" Additionally, the new transcription provides insight into the Kalinga tuning system in vocal music by investigating scholarship on anhemitonic scales in instrumental music.","Kalinga, Mabaka Valley",Austronesian
6,Kalinga Heritage and Indigenous Culture | PDF | Travel - Scribd,https://www.scribd.com/document/699393542/KALINGA-HERITAGE-NOTES,"This document provides an overview of the historical, cultural, and linguistic features of the Kalinga people in the northern Philippines. It discusses how the Kalinga and other Cordillera peoples are believed to have migrated to the region from Southeast or East Asia. It then describes the creation and settlements of the eight municipalities of Kalinga province, highlighting their boundaries ...","Kalinga, Mabaka Valley",Austronesian
7,Item - Na Suklit: Benicio Sokkong and the Bamboo Musical ... - figshare,https://openaccess.wgtn.ac.nz/articles/thesis/Na_Suklit_Benicio_Sokkong_and_the_Bamboo_Musical_Instruments_of_the_Kalinga/16999252,"This ethnomusicology study explores the contexts of the bamboo musical instruments of the Kalinga people of the Philippines in two distinct contemporary locations: the urban setting of Lucnab, Baguio City, and the rural setting of Sukiap, Kalinga. Through the study of the instruments, the music, and the individuals who participate in the music, I will examine the fluid and reflexive ...","Kalinga, Mabaka Valley",Austronesian
8,KALINGA HERITAGE: An Overview of Culture and Ethnolinguistic ... - Studocu,https://www.studocu.com/ph/document/saint-louis-college/bachelors-in-secondary-education/kalinga-heritage-cordi-101/119675483,"The Mabaka Valley Kalingas, which inhabit the southeastern part of Kalinga, is also known as the Kal-Uwan, Mabaka, and Mabaka Itneg. The Madukayang Kalinga are concentrated in the southern Mountain Province.","Kalinga, Mabaka Valley",Austronesian
9,Kalinga Heritage and Cultural Overview | PDF - Scribd,https://www.scribd.com/document/685582983/KALINGA-HERITAGE,"The document provides an overview of the historical and cultural features of the Kalinga people in the Philippines, including their origins, the development of distinct ethnolinguistic groups in the Cordillera region, and how Kalinga has emerged as an eco-tourism destination since becoming a separate province in 1995. It also includes details about the individual municipalities that make up ...","Kalinga, Mabaka Valley",Austronesian
